1
00:00:00,102 --> 00:00:03,022
(Receptionist:)If you have to ask,
maybe you shouldn't be here.

2
00:00:03,981 --> 00:00:06,191
(Sheldon:)I think this is the place.

3
00:00:07,026 --> 00:00:08,356
- Fill these out.
- Thank you.

4
00:00:08,527 --> 00:00:10,697
(Leonard:)- We'll be right back.
- Oh, take your time.

5
00:00:10,863 --> 00:00:13,533
(Receptionist:)I'll just finish my crossword puzzle.

6
00:00:14,158 --> 00:00:16,368
(Receptionist:)Oh, wait.

7
00:00:26,587 --> 00:00:28,717
(Sheldon:)Leonard, I don't think I can do this.

8
00:00:28,881 --> 00:00:31,511
(Leonard:)What, are you kidding? You're a semipro.

9
00:00:32,176 --> 00:00:34,466
(Sheldon:)No. We are committing genetic fraud.

10
00:00:34,637 --> 00:00:37,847
There's no guarantee our sperm's
going to generate high-IQ offspring.

11
00:00:38,015 --> 00:00:39,015
(Sheldon:)Think about that.

12
00:00:39,183 --> 00:00:43,523
(Sheldon:)I have a sister with the same basic DNA mix
who hostesses at Fuddruckers.

13
00:00:44,146 --> 00:00:45,816
(Leonard:)Sheldon, this was your idea.

14
00:00:45,981 --> 00:00:49,191
(Leonard:)A little extra money to get
fractional T1 bandwidth in the apartment?

15
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:52,700
(Sheldon:)I know.
And I do yearn for faster downloads.

16
00:00:53,239 --> 00:00:56,199
(Sheldon:)There's some poor woman
who's gonna pin her hopes on my sperm.

17
00:00:56,367 --> 00:00:59,367
(Sheldon:)What if she winds up with a toddler
who doesn't know if he should use...

18
00:00:59,537 --> 00:01:03,037
...a differential to solve for the area
under a curve?

